entry.summary:
In the previous post we stood up a basic /ping health‑check endpoint to confirm our SAM project was wired correctly. Today we will build our first real piece of CRM functionality: a POST /contacts endpoint that stores a contact record in Amazon DynamoDB, now powered by AWS Lambda Powertools for structured logging, tracing, and metrics. Request POST /contacts { "email": "jane.doe@example.com", // required "name": "Jane Doe", // optional "phone": "+11234567890", // optional }
Response 201 Created { "id": "c8a5c3d1-2bfe-45d0-b7e3-6d1fb25ce9a7", "email": "jane.doe@example.com", "name": "Jane Doe", "phone": "+11234567890", "created_at": 1721340000, "updated_at": 1721340000 }
We return the full record, including generated fields such as id, created_…
